            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[# Cranach Catalog Finder 1.0.6

This release turns Cranach into a complete Mac application and brings more
focus to the package-building workspace:

- Cranach now opens in its own resizable app window with a Dock icon and normal
  Mac menus instead of launching the interface in a browser
- closing the Cranach window now quits the app cleanly and stops its private
  local catalog service; reopening the app starts the complete experience again
- Check for Updates is available from the Cranach Catalog Finder application
  menu as well as Settings
- typing on Home now moves the logo and navigation away in one soft transition,
  bringing search results and Your Selections together at the top of the window
- Your Selections has a centered empty state and a smaller, connected package
  details and save area at the bottom
- result cards now emphasize the product name and exact item number, use clearer
  descriptions and quieter catalog paths, and show readiness only when an item
  needs attention
- unfinished packages are saved in private Application Support storage so the
  native window and future app updates can restore them reliably
- downloads from the native window keep safe filenames and never overwrite an
  existing file in Downloads

Previously downloaded packages, client history, catalog reviews, and catalog
data remain in place during the update. A draft that was never downloaded and
exists only inside the old browser's storage cannot be moved automatically into
the new native window; drafts saved after this update use the durable app store.
]]></description>
